-- title:
--   Branch primes with distinct tangent lines contract to distinct stalk primes
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \mid M'$, and let $L$ be a characteristic-zero field that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{q\ell\}$, equipped with a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\xi$ satisfying $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the image of the $j$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), assumed nonzero, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $z$ be a point of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) at which the germ of (the global section coming from) $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y$ be a point of the finite chart $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin`, such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Suppose further given a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0, X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f$ congruent to the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0, X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ with respect to its maximal ideal onto $S := W[[X_0, X_1]]/(C(\sigma\varpi)v - fu)$. Then for all integers $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ such that neither contains both images of $X_0$ and $X_1$, both contain the image of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, each $P_i$ contains the image of $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ for some $h_i \in (X_0, X_1)^2$, and $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along the algebra map from the stalk to its adic completion followed by $e$ are distinct primes of the stalk.
--
--   This is the separation statement for the $q+1$ branches of the Drinfeld local chart at a supersingular point of the integral model: branches with distinct tangent directions modulo $q$ remain distinct after contracting to the (non-complete) local ring, the hypotheses on $W, \sigma, f, u, v, e$ being those of an arbitrary chart witness. It is used by the results that produce such a chart isomorphism of the completed stalk, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-type auxiliary level frame with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, where no lower bound on $q$ is imposed.
